.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_FORMAT
The output format when no flag names one:
.BR json ,
.BR plain ,
.BR table ,
.B treemap
or
.BR ndjson .
It wins over the agent and CI variables below.
.TP
.BR CLAUDECODE ", " CODEX_THREAD_ID ", " CODEX_VERSION ", " GEMINI_CLI
Set by an agent's shell: the output is the JSON envelope, even on a
terminal.
.TP
.B CI
Set (and not
.B 0
or
.BR false ):
the output is
.BR \-\-plain .
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_THREADS
The scanner's worker threads, as
.BR \-\-threads .
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_THEME
The treemap's colours, as
.BR \-\-theme :
a pack's name or the path of a theme file.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set and not empty: no colour. The treemap is drawn in shades.
.TP
.BR CLICOLOR_FORCE ", " FORCE_COLOR
Set (and not
.BR 0 ):
colour even when stdout is not a terminal.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
turns colour off.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.BR 24bit :
the treemap is drawn in 24\-bit colour; otherwise in the 256\-colour cube.
.TP
.B COLORFGBG
A light background (the last field 7 or 15) picks the light theme when
none is named.
.TP
.B LS_COLORS
The extension colours of
.BR "\-\-color\-by lscolors" .
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
Without UTF\-8 the treemap is drawn in ASCII.
.TP
.B TZ
The local zone that
.BR \-\-since " and " \-\-until
read a date in.
